	(text_box "Memory LCD LS013B7DH05 on 3V3_AON: last image (READY / NOT READY) stays while the device is off"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 214.295 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "12407a30-db79-5835-86c3-4d9ab4906676")
	)
	(text_box "Sharp LD-26912A: VDD/VDDA 2.7-3.3 V (3V3_AON, TPS70933 3.3 V), input high 2.7 V to VDD, operating -20 to +70 C at the panel. EXTMODE = H (tied to VDD): COM inversion from EXTCOMIN =\nRTC_CLKOUT, 1 Hz from the always-on RTC on 03. Sharp's 57-66 Hz EXTCOMIN figure applies only while data are written continuously (Remark 6-3/6-4); 1 Hz holds a static image (Fig 6-4 shows 1\nHz LC inversion).\nSPI from the main (LCD_SCLK, LCD_SI, LCD_SCS): 1 MOhm to GND on each (contract §5.8 default resistors: main off -> lines low -> SCS low, display holds its memory) and 1 kOhm series into the\npanel (limits current into the panel inputs if 3V3_MAIN is momentarily above 3V3_AON; input high must not exceed VDD, LD-26912A Table 5-1). 1 kOhm x about 10 pF = 10 ns against SCLK 1 MHz\nmax (twSCLKH 405 ns).\nExternal capacitors per LD-26912A §9: 1 uF on VDD, 1 uF on VDDA, 0.1 uF on DISP."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 214.295 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "74207d17-da47-55c8-a4c3-0df221d3ef06")
	)
	(text_box "Blanking: LCD_BLANK (high = blank) -> 74AUP1G04 on 3V3_AON -> DISP (R-21)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260.015 25.4 0)
		(size 148.755 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1a3c1ae2-5679-5ddf-9ba4-f5159ea0f361")
	)
	(text_box "Main off -> LCD_BLANK held low by R607 1 MOhm -> inverter output high -> DISP high = display ON showing memory. The AUP input has\nIoff (0.6 uA max with VCC = 0, SCES571K), so a powered main never back-feeds 3V3_AON and an unpowered main is never fed.\nR608 220 Ohm between the inverter and Sharp's recommended 0.1 uF on DISP: limits the charging current to (3.3 V / 220) = 15 mA,\ninside the AUP's +-20 mA output current rating [UNVERIFIED: abs. max. table not re-read]; DISP rise time becomes about 3 x 22 us\ninstead of Sharp's 50 ns figure, which the recommended 0.1 uF already makes unattainable."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260.015 31.75 0)
		(size 148.755 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a537db7b-0f21-50da-b583-f680b41a5590")
	)
	(text_box "Voice prompts and metronome: MAX98357A (I2S, mono mix) on 5V0_SYS, 28 mm 8 Ohm speaker"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260.015 85.185 0)
		(size 227.005 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f21dd81a-b10c-5eaf-917a-e4fb3a9ac1bb")
	)
	(text_box "I2S_BCLK / LRCLK / SD each through 4.7 kOhm (contract §5.8; R-21: with 5V0_SYS off and the main on, the amplifier's inputs cannot back-power 5V0_SYS; firmware also holds I2S low while EN_5V0 is low).\n4.7 k x 3 pF = 14 ns against BCLK 3.072 MHz (325 ns period).\nSD_MODE: AMP_SD_N (push-pull 3.3 V) through R612 634 kOhm (Table 6 'R_LARGE' for 3.3 V logic) into the internal 92-108 kOhm pull-down -> 0.38-0.50 V = between trip points B0 (0.355 max) and B1 (0.65\nmin) = (left + right)/2 mono mix; AMP_SD_N low = shutdown. 634 k also limits current into SD_MODE to 5 uA if 5V0_SYS is off. R613 100 kOhm to GND is the contract's default resistor (main off ->\nshutdown).\nGAIN_SLOT tied to VDD = +6 dB (Table 8). 0 dBFS -> 2.1 + 6 = 8.1 dBV = 2.54 Vrms -> 0.81 W into 8 Ohm (0.95 W at 6.8 Ohm, -15 %) = within the speaker's 1.0 W rating. Sound [CALC from PUI data]: 80 +-\n3 dB at 1 m / 1 W -> 79 +- 3 dB at 1 m at full scale. The parts-study target of 85 dB(A) at 1 m needs about 3.2 W into this speaker: NOT MET (capture notes, departure D-C1).\nVDD: 10 uF + 0.1 uF (data sheet 'Power-Supply Input'). Filterless output: speaker leads short, inductance of the voice coil > 10 uH required (data sheet); EP to GND plane. Operating range of the\nMAX98357A is -40 to +85 C."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 260.015 91.535 0)
		(size 227.005 21.431)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "91b26c49-be17-5639-885b-046d5b7e2287")
	)
	(text_box "Cancel: two sealed tactile switches under one guarded cap, CANCEL_M_N -> main, CANCEL_S_N -> supervisor (§B8.4)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 118.743 0)
		(size 191.48 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bd7bc077-17c3-56d9-b5e5-ab42b99f384e")
	)
	(text_box "Each contract: switch to GND, TVS at the switch (TPD1E10B06, 100 nA max leakage at 5 V), 1 kOhm series + 100 nF to GND. Pull-ups are on the readers' sheets (10 kOhm to\n3V3_MAIN on 04, 10 kOhm to 3V3_SUP on 05; contract §5.8). Release time constant (10 k + 1 k) x 100 nF = 1.1 ms; press discharges through 1 k in 0.1 ms; contact bounce <\n1 ms (C&K KSC data) is left to the controllers' debounce. 1 kOhm limits ESD current into the controller pin after the TVS.\nGold-contact KSC6 (contact material code 3) because the pull-up current is only 0.3 mA: the silver version's minimum current is 1 mA (C&K KSC sheet).\nThe two circuits share only GND; one cap presses both (mechanical, not drawn). D-31 stuck rule and M/S disagreement: §13 fault 37."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 125.093 0)
		(size 191.48 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "09067360-fec6-5486-9018-295b47970920")
	)
	(text_box "Adult/child switch, two-pole changeover (D-60): pole A to the main, pole B to the charger ceiling"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.2 199.326 0)
		(size 220.13 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "74173020-d158-5eb0-b8df-049975691750")
	)
	(text_box "Pole A (common to GND): CHILD throw -> MODE_CHILD_N, ADULT throw -> MODE_ADULT_N; pull-ups 10 kOhm on 04. Between positions or open: both high = fault (contract §5.8).\nPole B (common to 5V0_SYS): CHILD throw -> R622 1 kOhm -> MODE_CHILD_HW; ADULT throw unused. Closed only in CHILD: MODE_CHILD_HW = 5.0 V x 100 k / 101 k = 4.95 V (100 kOhm pull-down on 10).\nOpen, broken or between positions -> MODE_CHILD_HW low -> ADULT ceiling (D-60). R622 limits a short of the board-to-board wire to GND to 5 mA so it cannot pull 5V0_SYS down. C619 10 nF filters\nthe line (10 us).\nThe two poles are mechanically ganged; pins 1 and 4 (CHILD throws) sit on the same side of the switch so one slider position closes both (C&K JS DPDT circuit diagram: commons 2 and 5)\n[UNVERIFIED for the SMT JCQN variant, see capture notes].\nESD: TVS on each pole-A throw at the switch, 1 kOhm series + 10 nF to the controller (release 0.1 ms)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.2 205.676 0)
		(size 220.13 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b64b78bb-0e2d-5a4f-807b-3c60ef63c4a8")
	)
	(text_box "Power button PWR_BTN_N into the always-on wake logic (03) and the main (04)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
